From 0f0a9afabd9261d4efdcd0f8c102bcf732f02552 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Stoyan <andrey.stoyan.csam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:21:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 21/43] test(chexc): clause unions, finalizer exclusions,
 pessimistic cast targets

Covers the five rules fixed in the compiler this round:

- parse/decl_multiple_clauses.cj -- several 'throws'/'captures' clauses union,
  across a 'where' block too, with '...' repeating idempotently.
- parse/neg_empty_clause_combined.cj -- 'throws () throws A' in both orders.
- parse/neg_empty_list_mixed.cj -- '()' nested in or mixed with other entries.
- parse/neg_finalizer_clause.cj and scopes/neg_finalizer.cj -- the clause side and
  the scope side of the finalizer rule; they are separate files because the clause
  error is a type-check error and aborts before the capability pass runs, so the
  demand cases would never be reached.
- inference/neg_ellipsis_exported.cj -- '...' on public, protected and interface
  declarations.
- types/cast_pessimistic.cj and types/cast_pessimistic_neg.cj -- the requirement a
  cast hands back, discharged and undischarged, through both 'as' and a type
  pattern, with the contravariant positions staying clause-free.
- types/cast_target_neg.cj -- targets with no sound reading (ArrayList, Option,
  Array of a function type) and a clause written in a target.

parse/neg_duplicate_clause.cj is removed: the behaviour it pinned is now the
supported one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
